hi there  it's day  62  it's saint patrick's day i've never i  got my green shirt on i have never  figured out why st patrick's day is so  popular in so many places  uh saint george is the patron saint of  england saint andrews the peyton's  patron saint of scotland and we don't  really celebrate those days  at least quite as universally as st  patrick's day  um  you know tomorrow i'm going to have an  hours conversation with jooheon i'm  going to record some of it just to show  you um i've really fallen off in my  korean i have to admit i went down to  san diego with my wife to play golf for  her birthday and then i've been  following this whole ukrainian  situation i'm still listening to more  russian  a little bit of ukrainian than to korean  um but i have been uh putting some  effort into um  kim yong-ha as i say to the podcast it's  very interesting  um took my uh son and his family off to  the airport last night so  his wife's mom has to look after the dog  and it's a it's a what is it a labrador  and uh some kind of a  spaniel i think so it needs to walk  twice a day so  i have to go in the afternoon and walk  the dog so it's been a busy day because  i played hockey this morning  and  normally we have  you know  basically  10 aside plus two goaltenders  but we only had five aside so we played  four on four hockey with one spare  uh that's a lot of work for an hour and  a half i was quite beat and then i had  to walk the dog for an hour a big strong  dog  so i'm quite tired but um  you know uh  one thing that's nice is i study  languages for fun i don't have any tests  so in a way tomorrow uh  meeting again with julian whom i haven't  spoken to for about three weeks or so  i have no idea how i'm going to do and i  don't care  uh it's not like preparing for a test  where you have to somehow work on those  structures or patterns that were taught  or covered in the previous chapters or  that vocabulary i'm not responsible for  anything i'm not responsible for the  vocabulary  that i  learned you know over the last little  while whatever whatever comes out comes  out  nice way to study i like that um  the other thing you know  i'm 68 gonna be 69 in october  so some people i'm sure who are young  who are 20 they think wow is that ever  old  let me tell you i don't feel old at all  um  you know play hockey uh whatever and i'm  lucky i guess in that sense that i have  no major health issues  um and the hockey group you know i was  just thinking about today is really a  very nice group of people they're all  between the ages of 65 and  72 really  uh there's some younger ones late 50s  we play hockey  uh one fellow  lost his wife to cancer  in fact a number have there have been  some people who have uh  had you know cancer or other  diseases both players or their wives  so this fellow uh lost his wife and then  he had an issue he was in the hospital  and so we got an email from one of the  guys who went to visit with him and  reported that he was in good spirits and  moved home in fact  and another guy had moved in with him  because he's alone had moved in with him  for a week just to help him out as he  came out of hospital  and then our guy was asked him if he  needed any food he said no because he's  got so much food that yet another person  had to lend him a refrigerator to store  all the food  so it's nice that i mean i have my  family i don't you know  rely on these other uh buddies uh so  much but it's nice to see that there is  this and there's a great spirit amongst  these guys some of whom have played  together for 30 or 40 years  so that's kind of nice  um  and yeah i enjoy my my language learning  i enjoy it because i do it for fun and i  don't think that i do worse than those  that are in programs where they're  required to  um  you know cram what they learned in the  last month in order to prepare for a an  exam  i can't wait till i  till i understand more of kim yoha  because he's talking about  uh you know venomous and ancient greece  and  you know french revolution and  literature and there's so much stuff  there i just get little snippets of  but i'm going out to do some more  so that's all you get today and tomorrow  unless i mess up on the technology  i should have a little korean  discussion with  with julion  bye for now

